WEBVTT

00:00:03.819 --> 00:00:10.119
<v Priya Raman>Morning, everyone. Monday, sixth of July. Can you hear me, or am I doing the Teams mime again?</v>

00:00:10.589 --> 00:00:15.839
<v Tomasz Nowak>We can hear you. Bit of an echo, but that might be this tin box.</v>

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:20.929
<v Marcus Hale>Before we start—did anyone see the football last night?</v>

00:00:22.109 --> 00:00:25.260
<v Sarah Okafor>Enough of it. Not sure I'd call that defending.</v>

00:00:25.719 --> 00:00:30.620
<v Marcus Hale>Exactly! Just stood there watching it go past. Could've put a traffic cone in.</v>

00:00:31.269 --> 00:00:34.770
<v Priya Raman>Right, football analysis concluded. Probably more successfully than the match.</v>

00:00:35.689 --> 00:00:43.039
<v Tomasz Nowak>And the heating in the portakabin—it's July and I was roasting in here. Not a maintenance request, just having a moan.</v>

00:00:44.369 --> 00:00:45.770
<v Fiona Doyle>A very seasonal moan.</v>

00:00:48.149 --> 00:00:52.000
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, well, we've got winter outside and August under the desk.</v>

00:00:54.079 --> 00:00:57.579
<v Priya Raman>Lovely. Let's separate what's finished from what we're actually agreeing.</v>

00:00:59.929 --> 00:01:05.879
<v Sarah Okafor>I've already swapped the filter on the chiller on three yesterday. That's done, not another filter job.</v>

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:10.530
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, finished work. I've got that separate from the outstanding sign-off.</v>

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:16.760
<v Tomasz Nowak>And I tested the cold unit yesterday and it's all fine now.</v>

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:20.870
<v Priya Raman>Good. No repeat test being added here.</v>

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:28.500
<v Sarah Okafor>Also, already swapped the filter on the hot bearing yesterday. That one's finished as well.</v>

00:01:29.099 --> 00:01:35.049
<v Marcus Hale>While we're on updates, I heard a slight rattle from the alarm box, nothing to action yet.</v>

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:44.450
<v Tomasz Nowak>Same sort of observation here—heard a slight rattle from the Line 2 Pick and Place Robot, nothing to action yet.</v>

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:49.909
<v Priya Raman>Okay, observations only, neither of those is a new job out of this meeting.</v>

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:57.310
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Um, my blocker hasn't moved. I can't get to the front end of one until production gives us a window.</v>

00:01:58.159 --> 00:02:03.060
<v Sarah Okafor>There isn't a window agreed. So that's still blocked, not a promise for today.</v>

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:08.430
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, exactly. Don't want it sounding as if I'm in there already.</v>

00:02:09.969 --> 00:02:12.770
<v Priya Raman>Right. What can we actually commit to, then?</v>

00:02:14.409 --> 00:02:19.310
<v Olumide Adeyemi>I'll do the pre-use checks on the counterbalances by end of day. It's urgent.</v>

00:02:20.599 --> 00:02:26.199
<v Grace Liu>Pre-use being the important bit there—not running them first and catching up with the checks afterwards.</v>

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:32.770
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Absolutely. Before use. End of day is the outer deadline for getting the checks done.</v>

00:02:34.319 --> 00:02:37.120
<v Priya Raman>Thanks, Mide. Urgent, by end of day, agreed.</v>

00:02:39.599 --> 00:02:46.599
<v Marcus Hale>I'll chase the purchase order for the GT2 Number 2 Bearing by the 28th. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:54.090
<v Fiona Doyle>That's the PO chase, rather than promising the bearing will be here by the 28th?</v>

00:02:54.639 --> 00:02:59.189
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, the chase. I'm not giving you a delivery date I haven't got.</v>

00:02:59.689 --> 00:03:03.539
<v Priya Raman>Fine, Marc. Purchase order chase by the 28th; important, not urgent.</v>

00:03:05.669 --> 00:03:08.469
<v Fiona Doyle>Good. Those two things get muddled surprisingly easily.</v>

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:16.379
<v Grace Liu>I'll write up the near miss at the pop valve. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:03:18.379 --> 00:03:21.879
<v Sarah Okafor>The write-up, yeah. We're not describing a live emergency here.</v>

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:26.550
<v Grace Liu>Exactly, the near-miss account. That's what I'm taking.</v>

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:31.840
<v Priya Raman>Thanks, Grace Liu. Agreed, no deadline being added to that.</v>

00:03:33.199 --> 00:03:37.400
<v Tomasz Nowak>Sorry, caught half of that over the fan. Got it now—the write-up.</v>

00:03:39.879 --> 00:03:44.080
<v Priya Raman>And I'll book a contractor to look at the HRSG this morning.</v>

00:03:45.349 --> 00:03:50.250
<v Fiona Doyle>Pri, that's making the booking this morning, not the contractor turning up this morning?</v>

00:03:52.719 --> 00:03:56.219
<v Priya Raman>Yes, booking this morning. I'm not promising an attendance time.</v>

00:03:58.330 --> 00:03:59.729
<v Marcus Hale>Right, that makes sense.</v>

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:11.740
<v Priya Raman>Marc, can you do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the chiller on three? The due phrase on this is on the 3rd, and that one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:04:13.139 --> 00:04:17.339
<v Marcus Hale>Sorry, no, I can't take that sign-off. Don't put it against me.</v>

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:24.319
<v Fiona Doyle>Just to be clear, on the 3rd is already past. We're not quietly moving it to a future date?</v>

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:35.579
<v Priya Raman>Correct. It was due on the 3rd; it's outstanding. Saz, can you take the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the chiller on three instead? That one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:04:38.009 --> 00:04:43.959
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, I'll take it. Due on the 3rd, still outstanding, and I'll do the sign-off straight away.</v>

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:49.399
<v Grace Liu>And the filter being finished doesn't stand in for the isolation sign-off. Separate things.</v>

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:55.660
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, absolutely. I wasn't claiming the filter swap closed that out.</v>

00:04:57.079 --> 00:05:00.579
<v Priya Raman>Good. Saz has the sign-off, not Marc. Safety-critical, straight away.</v>

00:05:02.279 --> 00:05:07.879
<v Priya Raman>Also, boss, can you do a site visit at Northfield Substation with the contractor? Normal priority.</v>

00:05:09.569 --> 00:05:13.769
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, I'll do the site visit at Northfield Substation with the contractor.</v>

00:05:16.019 --> 00:05:19.870
<v Fiona Doyle>Normal priority, and there's no visit date agreed in this discussion.</v>

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:22.279
<v Priya Raman>That's right. No extra date attached.</v>

00:05:22.649 --> 00:05:27.899
<v Priya Raman>Haley, can you recalibrate the sensors on the little water valve on two? Normal priority.</v>

00:05:28.209 --> 00:05:33.459
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, I'll recalibrate the sensors on the little water valve on two. Normal priority, understood.</v>

00:05:35.199 --> 00:05:38.000
<v Olumide Adeyemi>The sensor calibration, not changing the valve itself.</v>

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:42.829
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, just the sensors. No valve replacement sneaking onto the list.</v>

00:05:44.649 --> 00:05:51.300
<v Sarah Okafor>And I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the new line tomorrow morning. Fairly important, that one.</v>

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:55.089
<v Grace Liu>Both parts—the permit to work and the isolation?</v>

00:05:55.949 --> 00:05:58.399
<v Sarah Okafor>Both, yes. I'll sort them tomorrow morning.</v>

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:02.750
<v Priya Raman>Cheers, boss. Fairly important, tomorrow morning, agreed.</v>

00:06:04.639 --> 00:06:10.939
<v Priya Raman>Last one: safety Grace, can you grease and check the bearings on the air compressor Monday? No rush.</v>

00:06:11.279 --> 00:06:16.529
<v Grace Liu>Yes, I'll grease and check the bearings on the air compressor Monday. No rush, understood.</v>

00:06:17.529 --> 00:06:22.430
<v Fiona Doyle>Monday being today, just so that doesn't end up looking like next week's work.</v>

00:06:24.089 --> 00:06:27.939
<v Priya Raman>Yes, today, Monday. Still no rush; that's the priority we've agreed.</v>

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:31.579
<v Grace Liu>Fine by me. Grease and bearing check, both covered.</v>

00:06:32.889 --> 00:06:38.139
<v Tomasz Nowak>Nothing else from me. Mine were the finished test and the observation, not extra jobs.</v>

00:06:39.449 --> 00:06:43.649
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And the access blocker stays a blocker. Apart from that, all clear.</v>

00:06:45.009 --> 00:06:50.610
<v Priya Raman>Right, that's us. Thanks, everyone. And please spare us the football replay in the next call.</v>
